I actually just read (and write) ROT-13. It's not all that hard to learn
(as Klaus conjectured at one point). Since the characters go in pairs, and
adjacent characters encode adjacent characters, recognizing rstln and the
vowels gives you 18 letters you can recognize, and the other 8 are
adjacent to ones you know. With a little practice you can recognize the
common words, and you can generally guess a long word from the first few
letters and the last letter without reading the middle.

Alternatively, you could find fonts with vfb10646-1 encoding and a djregl
keyboard...

